    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Emails that ask you to do something become Notion tasks (AI)\nAI reads each new email; when it asks you to do something, a task with a due date and context is created in your Notion database.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e2a17d1b-0672-5d07-9291-06bc8fe1ab8e",
      "name": "Note: what this does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. In Notion, create a database (a table) and an internal integration at notion.so/my-integrations. Share the database with the integration (... > Connections).\n2. Add a Notion credential in n8n with the integration secret (you paste it). Open **Settings** and paste the database URL.\n3. Connect Gmail and OpenAI. Only emails that really ask you to do something become tasks.\n4. Test once, check the new page in Notion, then switch to **Active**.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "43114848-1809-5389-8c38-089bb7f0f056",
      "name": "Note: setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        400,
        -420
      ]
    }
